\documentclass{article}
\title{Batch Correction for Single-Cell RNA Sequencing}
\author{Maria Chen}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Methods}
Raw reads were aligned to the reference genome with STAR. Cells with fewer than 200 detected genes were discarded. Count matrices were normalized by total counts and log-transformed. Highly variable genes were selected with the dispersion-based method. Batch effects were corrected with our proposed algorithm, and clustering was performed on the corrected embedding.
\section{Results}
Our method removes batch effects while preserving biological variation.
\end{document}
